Subtask 1.2: Configure Database High Availability
Set up PostgreSQL streaming replication for database high availability.

Configure PostgreSQL on the primary server:
# Stop Satellite services
sudo satellite-maintain service stop

# Configure PostgreSQL for replication
sudo -u postgres psql -c "CREATE USER replicator REPLICATION LOGIN ENCRYPTED PASSWORD 'replicator_password';"

# Edit PostgreSQL configuration
sudo vi /var/lib/pgsql/data/postgresql.conf
Add these configurations to postgresql.conf:

# Replication settings
wal_level = replica
max_wal_senders = 3
max_replication_slots = 3
archive_mode = on
archive_command = 'cp %p /var/lib/pgsql/archive/%f'
hot_standby = on
Configure pg_hba.conf for replication:
sudo vi /var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf
Add this line:

host replication replicator satellite-secondary/32 md5
Create archive directory and restart PostgreSQL:
sudo mkdir -p /var/lib/pgsql/archive
sudo chown postgres:postgres /var/lib/pgsql/archive
sudo systemctl restart postgresql
Subtask 1.3: Set Up Secondary Database Server
Configure the secondary server as a PostgreSQL standby.

Prepare the secondary server:
# On satellite-secondary
sudo dnf install -y postgresql-server postgresql-contrib

# Stop PostgreSQL if running
sudo systemctl stop postgresql

# Remove default data directory
sudo rm -rf /var/lib/pgsql/data/*
Create base backup from primary:
# On satellite-secondary
sudo -u postgres pg_basebackup -h satellite-primary -D /var/lib/pgsql/data -U replicator -P -v -R -W
Configure standby server:
# Create recovery configuration
sudo -u postgres vi /var/lib/pgsql/data/postgresql.conf
Add these settings:

hot_standby = on
primary_conninfo = 'host=satellite-primary port=5432 user=replicator password=replicator_password'
Start PostgreSQL on secondary:
sudo systemctl enable --now postgresql

# Verify replication status
sudo -u postgres psql -c "SELECT * FROM pg_stat_replication;"
Subtask 1.4: Configure Load Balancer
Set up HAProxy for load balancing between Satellite servers.

Install and configure HAProxy:
