# Satellite Disaster Recovery Procedures

## Pre-Disaster Checklist
- [ ] Verify backup integrity
- [ ] Document current system state
- [ ] Ensure secondary systems are ready
- [ ] Test communication channels

## Disaster Recovery Steps
1. Assess damage and determine recovery strategy
2. Prepare recovery environment
3. Restore database from backup
4. Restore configuration files
5. Restart services and verify functionality
6. Update DNS and load balancer configuration
7. Validate client connectivity

## Recovery Time Objectives (RTO)
- Database restoration: 2 hours
- Full system recovery: 4 hours
- Client reconnection: 1 hour

## Recovery Point Objectives (RPO)
- Database: 24 hours (daily backups)
- Configuration: 7 days (weekly backups)
Create database restoration script:
sudo vi /usr/local/bin/satellite-db-restore.sh
#!/bin/bash
# Satellite Database Restoration Script

if [ $# -ne 1 ]; then
    echo "Usage: $0 <backup_date>"
    echo "Example: $0 20231201_020000"
    exit 1
fi

BACKUP_DATE=$1
BACKUP_DIR="/backup/database/$BACKUP_DATE"

if [ ! -d "$BACKUP_DIR" ]; then
    echo "Backup directory not found: $BACKUP_DIR"
    exit 1
fi

echo "Starting database restoration from $BACKUP_DATE..."

# Stop Satellite services
satellite-maintain service stop

# Drop and recreate databases
sudo -u postgres psql -c "DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS foreman;"
sudo -u postgres psql -c "DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS candlepin;"
sudo -u postgres psql -c "CREATE DATABASE foreman OWNER foreman;"
sudo -u postgres psql -c "CREATE DATABASE candlepin OWNER candlepin;"

# Restore databases
echo "Restoring Foreman database..."
gunzip -c $BACKUP_DIR/foreman_$BACKUP_DATE.sql.gz | sudo -u postgres psql -d foreman

echo "Restoring Candlepin database..."
gunzip -c $BACKUP_DIR/candlepin_$BACKUP_DATE.sql.gz | sudo -u postgres psql -d candlepin

# Start services
satellite-maintain service start

echo "Database restoration completed successfully!"
